WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.887
Dry fabric.

00:00:01.927 --> 00:00:03.455
And a little resin.

00:00:03.495 --> 00:00:06.832
How do they become a light, strong composite
panel?

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.525
Give us one minute.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.528
You need a mould.

00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:12.379
A resin pot.

00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:15.360
A vacuum pump that pulls out the air.

00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:18.498
A buffer tank that keeps the vacuum steady.

00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:21.275
And a resin trap that protects the pump.

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:23.213
Now the layers.

00:00:23.263 --> 00:00:27.212
Release agent, so the part comes off the mould
cleanly.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.314
Reinforcement fabrics, laid in the right
directions.

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:33.722
Peel ply and flow mesh.

00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:38.332
Resin enters at one edge; at the other, we pull
out the air.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.610
Finally, sealant tape and the vacuum bag.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.658
Vacuum on:

00:00:42.698 --> 00:00:45.540
the bag pulls tight over the layers.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.565
The valve opens, and air pressure pushes the
resin in.

00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:52.499
It soaks the fabrics – then it cures.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:54.267
Demoulding.

00:00:54.318 --> 00:00:59.869
Bag, mesh and peel ply come off in one piece,
and the finished panel releases from the mould.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:01.924
That's the recipe.

00:01:01.974 --> 00:01:04.122
Composites, explained.

